  "name": null,
  "problem": "Write the expression for the Riemann sum from part 7 in sigma notation.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The right Riemann sum $\\,=\\,0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-$  \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         ${i}^{2})$",
  "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+i\u0394x$ and $\u0394x=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nIn our case, we have $n=4$ subintervals, $a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $\u0394x=0.5.$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+i\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 0.5)\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0.5i) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-{(0.5i)}^{2}) \\\\  & =0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4-0.25{i}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
